{"availability":"available","full":"tmfreiberg/euclids-algorithm-analysis","name":"euclids-algorithm-analysis","description":"How many steps does Euclid's algorithm take, and how are those step counts distributed? A large-scale numerical study that sheds light on an elusive constant in the variance.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-05-05T16:18:01Z","updated":"2026-08-29T02:06:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tmfreiberg.github.io/euclids-algorithm-analysis/","topics":["algorithms","analysis-algorithms","art-of-computer-programming","data-visualization","gcd-calculator","knuth","matplotlib","numpy","pandas","scipy","time-complexity-analysis","time-complexity-visualization"],"demo":"https://tmfreiberg.github.io/euclids-algorithm-analysis/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:20.578Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:20.578Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:20.578Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:37:20.578Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["How many division steps does Euclid's algorithm take, on average, and how are those step counts distributed? This project implements Euclid's algorithm several ways, tabulates the step count T(a, b) over billions of integer pairs, and compares the empirical distributions against the asymptotic (Gaussian) behaviour predicted by the theorems of Heilbronn–Porter, Norton, Hensley, and Baladi–Vallée — including an empirical estimate of the otherwise-unknown subdominant constant κ ≈ −0.1 in the variance.","📖 The full exposition — mathematics, code, plots, and animations — is published as a Quarto book:","This repository holds the reusable Python package (euclidanalysis), its test suite, the precomputed data and figures, and the sources for that book."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tmfreiberg/euclids-algorithm-analysis/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint